      "title": "POSITIF - instruction d'edition",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.3.56",
        "Node name for S&R": "TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Reference image 1 is the scene to preserve. Reference image 2 is the fixed character identity reference — use it only to correct the face, never for pose, framing, lighting, clothing or background.\n\nKeep 100% unchanged from image 1: pose, body, clothing, hairstyle, framing, background, lighting direction, overall atmosphere, and the current skin texture and finish exactly as they are — do not smooth, re-light or re-render the skin.\n\nOnly correct the face to match image 2's identity where image 1 has drifted from it:\n- Eyebrow shape and thickness — restore the fuller, more natural brow shape from image 2 if image 1's brows read as thinner or more groomed.\n- Eye color and shape — match image 2 exactly.\n- Freckle pattern — match placement and density from image 2 (nose, cheeks), keeping them sitting on top of image 1's existing skin texture.\n- Overall face structure (jaw, nose, mouth proportions) — align with image 2 if it has drifted.\n\nDo not change expression, gaze direction, or head angle from image 1.\n\nPhotorealistic, vertical, same composition and crop as image 1."
      ],
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    },
